HENK: your app answered — with an error.

This one isn't henk. DNS, routing, the certificate and the dev server are
all working: henk forwarded the request, and your app handed back a server
error. The fix is in your app, not in the proxy.

Where to look:

  1. The terminal running your dev server.
     The stack trace is there — henk only relays the status code, it never
     sees the exception.

  2. Your app's own logs.
     storage/logs/laravel.log, docker compose logs -f, or whatever your
     framework writes to.

Nothing to change in henk — `henk doctor` will confirm the routing is
healthy if you want to rule it out.
